course: dictionary
lesson: 7873
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word raise has many meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one you need. Read the clues before you choose. «Raise your hand if you know the answer.» Here raise means lift, or move higher. Check: does "lift your hand" fit the sentence? Yes, so that meaning is right.
explain: The words near raise are the clues. «The farmers raise sheep on the hill» does not mean they lift the sheep. The farmers look after the sheep while they grow up. «The school wants to raise money for new books» means the school wants to collect money for a cause.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «Sam raised a question about the homework» fits with "mentioned a question," but "lifted a question" makes no sense. The sentence tells you the meaning, not the single word on its own.
explain: Raise also shows up in phrases such as raise your voice, which means speak louder, and raise the alarm, which means warn people of danger. When a phrase has a meaning that is different from its single words, the whole phrase is the clue.
fact: Raise is a verb: raise, raises, raised, raising.
fact: «A fever is when the body raises its temperature to fight infection.» Here raises means makes higher.
fact: In maths, «2 raised to the power 3» means 2 × 2 × 2 = 8.
fact: Raise your voice means speak louder, and raise the alarm means warn people of danger.
fact: In American English, a raise is an increase in pay.
exercise: «Raise your hand if you know the answer.» What does raise mean here? | Throw away | Wrap up | *Lift higher | Put to sleep
exercise: «The farmers raise sheep on the hill.» What does raise mean? | To lift them off the ground | *To look after them while they grow up | To sell them all at once | To count them every day
exercise: The school wants to raise money for new books. What does raise mean? | To hide money in a box | To spend money quickly | *To collect money for a cause | To lose money on purpose
test: «Sam's teacher raised a question about the homework.» What does raised mean? | Lifted a chair | Made the homework longer | Lowered the lights | *Mentioned a problem
test: In maths, what is 2 raised to the power 3? | *8 | 5 | 9 | 6
exam: In American English, what is a raise? | A loud voice | A day off school | *An increase in pay | A very tall building
